    feat(bootstrap): add secret inputs for managed files (#11680)

    <sub>Stack created with <a
    href="https://github.com/github/gh-stack">GitHub Stacks CLI</a> • <a
    href="https://gh.io/stacks-feedback">Give Feedback 💬</a></sub>

    ## Summary
    - declare logical bootstrap secret inputs backed by environment
    variables
    - add explicit masked prompting and non-revealing status output
    - add opt-in managed-file templates with `secret(name="...")`
    - integrate naturally with `fnox exec -- mise bootstrap ...` without
    provider coupling
    - preflight required values before full-bootstrap mutations and honor
    `--only`/`--skip files`
    - redact resolved and prompted values from mise output

    ## Security model
    - mise stores declarations, never provider credentials or secret values
    - plans, dry runs, status, and privileged-helper output never contain
    rendered content
    - prompted values remain process-local and are not exported
    - there is no secret reveal command
    - missing, empty, or non-Unicode inputs fail closed before file
    convergence

    ## Validation
    - `cargo test --bin mise system::secrets`
    - `cargo test --bin mise cli::command_effects`
    - `mise run test:e2e e2e/cli/test_bootstrap_secrets
    e2e/cli/test_bootstrap_system_files`
    - `mise run --force render`
    - `mise run lint-fix`
    - `cargo clippy --workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`

    *AI-assisted — Tool: Codex; model: openai/gpt-5; version: unavailable.*

    <!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->
    ---

    > [!NOTE]
    > **High Risk**
    > Changes bootstrap provisioning, privileged file content, and secret
    handling with fail-closed preflight; misconfiguration or redaction gaps
    could leave hosts partially provisioned or expose secrets in logs.
    >
    > **Overview**
    > Adds **`[bootstrap.secrets]`** so bootstrap can reference sensitive
    values via environment variables without storing them in config. Managed
    files gain **`template = true`** and **`{{ secret(name="...") }}`** for
    opt-in rendering; only secrets referenced by selected templates are
    required.
    >
    > **`mise bootstrap secrets status`** reports availability (never
    values). **`--prompt-secrets`** prompts securely for missing inputs on
    bootstrap, plan, files apply/status, and aggregate status. Full
    bootstrap **preflights** secret resolution before the files phase when
    files are not skipped.
    >
    > Plans and **`--detailed-exitcode`** now treat **`unknown`** resources
    (e.g. unavailable secrets) as planning failures. Status/plan paths use
    **`status_requests_from_config`** so missing secrets surface as unknown
    without leaking content; resolved values are redacted from output.
